# health v2.8 — clinical:status on an allergy record, IN
# AllergyIntolerance.clinicalStatus.
#
# THREE codes, not four: active | inactive | resolved. This fixture uses
# "inactive", and it carries clinical:verificationStatus "confirmed" alongside
# it, because the pair is what shows the two axes are separate elements with
# separate value sets. The allergy verification set has four codes and contains
# neither "provisional" nor "differential" -- a differential diagnosis is not a
# thing one has about an allergy -- which is why clinical v1.16 dropped
# clinical:verificationStatus's rdfs:domain clinical:Condition rather than
# widening it to a union: the same predicate binds to different value sets on
# different classes, and that is a SHACL job.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:a11e0208-0000-4000-8000-000000000001> a health:AllergyRecord ;
    health:allergen "Amoxicillin" ;
    health:reaction "Urticaria" ;
    clinical:status "inactive" ;
    clinical:verificationStatus "confirmed" ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
